# Helm API — local environment
#
# Bun reads apps/api/.env (generated). Do not hand-edit .env.
#
# Setup with 1Password CLI (recommended):
#   1. op signin
#   2. Copy the block that fits your Product into apps/api/.env.<product>
#      (see "Product input files" below). Set your absolute paths and
#      secret references.
#   3. pnpm sync-env -- <product>
#   4. pnpm dev
#
# <product> is a slug: lowercase letters, digits and hyphens, starting with a
# letter or digit, at most 64 characters (for example: helm, acme-platform).
# "example" is reserved for this template.
#
# Secret values live in 1Password. In the product files use references:
#   op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
# Never paste raw tokens into the product files.
#
# Without 1Password: copy a product block into .env and replace op://… with
# real values (not recommended).
#
# ─── Variables ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# HELM_KNOWLEDGE_REPO_PATH  Absolute path to the Product knowledge repo
#                           (directory that contains .helm/product.yaml).
# HELM_DATA_DIR             Absolute path to Helm operational data/.
# GITHUB_TOKEN              GitHub PAT (Projects + repo API).
# GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET     Shared secret for GitHub → Helm webhooks.
# LINEAR_API_KEY            Linear PAT — only when the Product uses Linear
#                           (issue_tracker.provider: linear). Helm-the-product
#                           uses GitHub Projects and does not need this key.
# LINEAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET     Shared secret for Linear → Helm webhooks (Linear
#                           Products only).
#
# ─── Product input files (gitignored; used by sync-env) ──────────────────────
#
# Create apps/api/.env.<product>, then:  pnpm sync-env -- <product>
#
# --- .env.<product> (a Product tracked in Linear) ---
# HELM_KNOWLEDGE_REPO_PATH=/Users/you/Git/example-org/example-knowledge
# HELM_DATA_DIR=/Users/you/Git/example-org/helm-data
# GITHUB_TOKEN=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
# LINEAR_API_KEY=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
# GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
# LINEAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
#
# --- .env.helm (Helm self-dogfood / GitHub Projects) ---
# HELM_KNOWLEDGE_REPO_PATH=/Users/you/Git/helm-knowledge
# HELM_DATA_DIR=/Users/you/Git/helm/apps/api/data
# GITHUB_TOKEN=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
# GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
